-- statement:
--   **`segLineC` computes the sparse segmented inverse** (real part, one line).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegLn8`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.segLineC_eq (hl : 1 ≤ lam) (hs : 0 < s) (hws : 2 * w < s) (hwK : w ≤ K)
--       (hKm : 2 * K + 1 ≤ (LJ s t lam w).length) {nc : ℕ} (hsN : s ≤ nc * lam) {x : List ℤ}
--       (hx : nc * lam ≤ x.length) {u : ℕ} (hu : u < nc * lam) :
--       (segLineC P R s t lam w α K nc x).getD u 0 =
--         if u < s then segInvS P lam (TT P R s t α) (BB s t lam w) (fun v => x.getD v 0) u else 0
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Segmented inverse (S2), machine side 8: one real line of `segInvS` by list kernels
--
--   The real part of the segmented inverse on one line, as the machine computes it, on a padded
--   line `x` of `N = n_c λ` positions (`s ≤ N`):
--
--   1. `Y = applyL x`: the chunk kernel on each `λ`-chunk (`M⁻¹`);
--   2. the values of `Y` on the line `L = Jlist B`, the two capacitance kernels (`jsolve_eq`);
--   3. the coupling window kernel on the cyclic extension (`couple_window`), scattered back to the
--      positions (zero off `L`);
--   4. `Y₂ = applyL` of the scattered coupling; the output is `Y - Y₂`.
--
--   **`segLineC_eq`**: entry `u < N` of the result is `segInvS … u` for `u < s` and `0` beyond.
